# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal data & generated output — NEVER commit these.
# We keep the folder structure + the placeholder README.md files so the repo
# ships with empty intake/output folders, but ignore everything you add to them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# data/ intake — your raw exports, organized by entity:
#   data/personal/<identity>/<source>/…   data/company/<company>/<source>/…
# Ship ONLY the neutral structural placeholder READMEs; NEVER descend into a real
# entity export folder. (A broad `!data/**/README.md` would re-include a README that
# ships INSIDE a real export, and would track your own data/personal/<you>/ folder —
# so we whitelist exact placeholder paths instead.)
data/**
!data/README.md
!data/personal/
!data/personal/README.md
!data/personal/your-name/
!data/personal/your-name/**/
!data/personal/your-name/**/README.md
!data/company/
!data/company/README.md
!data/company/your-company/
!data/company/your-company/**/
!data/company/your-company/**/README.md

# vault/ output — your generated brain(s):
#   vault/personal/<id>-brain/  vault/company/<co>-brain/  vault/_correlations/
#   vault/_profile/  (schema map + mindmap + brain-structure design)
# Keep only the placeholder README.
vault/**
!vault/README.md

# dist/ — built skills. Track ONLY the installable .skill zips (one per provider);
# ignore the unpacked dist/<provider>/second-brain-link/ build trees (they just
# duplicate engine/ and are regenerated by packaging/build_skill.py).
dist/**
!dist/
!dist/*/
!dist/**/*.skill

# Stray exports / per-build artifacts anywhere else
*.zip
*-vault/
my-second-brain/
schema_map.json
schema_map.md
mapping_overrides.json
_BUILD_REPORT.md
_COVERAGE.md
_SUMMARY.md
_STRUCTURE.md
_DOCTOR.md
_ERROR.md
Dashboard.md
_DATA_POINTS.md
_GRAPH.md
95-goals/
copilot-prompts/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.obsidian/
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local agent state (not the tracked .github/ — these are per-machine config)
.claude/
.claudian/

# Secrets / credentials — never commit. This is an offline tool that needs none of
# these, so the block is a pure safety net for anything you drop into the tree.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
.netrc
credentials*.json
client_secret*.json
service-account*.json
*secret*.json
*token*.json
*.log
